o_Polo"}],"approximate":"Historians reconstruct the route from the book; places are approximate and some are debated. Drawn on today's roads and sea lanes.","km":28431,"bbox":[12.3346,5.179,118.6724,45.4372],"stopCount":20,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Venezia_aerial_view.jpg/500px-Venezia_aerial_view.jpg","page":"Venice","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venezia_aerial_view.jpg","credit":"kallerna","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},"overview":[[45.4372,12.3346],[45.4372,12.3346]]},{"id":"a-time-of-gifts","title":"A Time of Gifts: on foot to Constantinople","who":"Patrick Leigh Fermor","when":"1933–1935","vehicle":"On foot (and the odd lift)","kind":"walk","color":"#9f1239","summary":"At eighteen, Patrick Leigh Fermor walks from the Hook of Holland to Constantinople, sleeping in barns, monasteries and castles across a Europe on the eve of war. His books, written decades later, are among the finest travel writing ever.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: A Time of Gifts","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Time_of_Gifts"}],"approximate":"Main places from his three books; the paths between them are approximate.","km":3319,"bbox":[4.1312,41.0059,28.9744,51.9773],"stopCount":14,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Hoek_van_Holland_town_centre.jpg/500px-Hoek_van_Holland_town_centre.jpg","page":"Hook of Holland","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hoek_van_Holland_town_centre.jpg","credit":"Cmglee","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"overview":[[51.9773,4.1312],[51.5504,6.5519],[49.8353,8.6332],[48.9734,8.4381],[48.5348,9.6541],[48.1359,17.1598],[47.6336,17.6623],[47.4822,19.1442],[47.8487,21.139],[47.0371,21.9145],[46.7696,23.5906],[45.9825,23.5435],[45.4615,22.2295],[43.1343,22.5716],[42.3269,23.9645],[41.0059,28.9744]]},{"id":"thomas-stevens","title":"Around the World on a Bicycle","who":"Thomas Stevens","when":"1884–1886","vehicle":"Columbia penny-farthing (high-wheeler)","ki