],[31.333,-108.5302]]},{"id":"transamerica-trail","title":"TransAmerica Bike Trail","who":"Classic touring route (Bikecentennial, 1976)","when":"Since 1976","vehicle":"Touring or road bike","kind":"bike","color":"#be123c","summary":"About 6,800 km coast to coast on quiet roads, from the Pacific in Oregon to the Atlantic in Virginia, through the Cascades, Yellowstone, the Rockies, the plains, the Ozarks and Appalachia. Created for America's bicentennial, when thousands rode it.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: TransAmerica Trail (bicycle)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TransAmerica_Trail_(bicycle)"}],"approximate":"Towns on the route; the line between them is approximate (use the official maps to ride it).","km":6167,"bbox":[-123.8318,36.5702,-76.5079,46.8776],"stopCount":16,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Astoria_Oregon.jpg/500px-Astoria_Oregon.jpg","page":"Astoria, Oregon","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astoria_Oregon.jpg","credit":"BeachcombersNW","license":"CC BY 2.0"},"overview":[[46.1882,-123.8318],[45.5083,-122.7797],[44.9163,-122.9912],[44.2909,-121.5492],[44.7749,-117.8344],[44.216,-116.9863],[46.1449,-115.9784],[46.8701,-113.9953],[46.5817,-112.9001],[46.0105,-112.7087],[45.7367,-111.7956],[44.9698,-111.6424],[44.7819,-111.1133],[44.0227,-111.4386],[42.7432,-109.7172],[41.6062,-109.2293],[41.7395,-106.8293],[39.245,-106.0373],[38.4354,-105.2533],[37.9859,-103.558],[38.0469,-97.3451],[37.6777,-97.1846],[37.1928,-93.5829],[38.6324,-90.1482],[38.3893,-89.3711],[37.7315,-89.2461],[37.765,-87.1648],[37.3841,-86.6529],[37.7971,-85.4283],[37.5687,-84.2963],[36.7312,-83.6689],[36.5776,-82.5082],[37.1259,-80.3784],[38.1191,-79.0489],[37.2381,-76.5079]]},{"id":"carretera-austral","title":"Carretera Austral","who":"Classic bikepacking and moto route","when":"Best in the southern summer","vehicle":"Touring, gravel or mountain bike; also motorcycles","kind":"bike","color":"#0369a1","summary":"About 1,200 km of Chile's Route 7 through northern Patagonia: rainforest, fjords, glaciers and turquoise rivers, with ferries and long gravel stretches. A dream ride for cyclists and riders alike.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Carretera Austral","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carretera_Austral"}],"approximate":"Main places on the road; ferry timetables change, so check before you go.","km":1198,"bbox":[-73.3385,-48.4685,-71.8345,-41.4715],"stopCount":11,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Montaje_de_Puerto_Montt.jpg/500px-Montaje_de_Puerto_Montt.jpg","page":"Puerto Montt","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montaje_de_Puerto_Montt.jpg","credit":"Montaje realizado por Wikiedro.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},"overview":[[-41.4715,-72.9397],[-41.9661,-72.4707],[-44.4886,-72.5839],[-45.9157,-71.8345],[-46.1913,-72.8037],[-47.2545,-72.5733],[-47.7832,-73.3062],[-48.4685,-72.5598]]},{"id":"camino-frances","title":"Camino de Santiago (Camino Francés)","who":"Classic pilgrimage route","when":"Walked since the Middle Ages","vehicle":"On foot (or by bike)","kind":"walk","color":"#ca8a04","summary":"About 780 km across northern Spain to the cathedral of Santiago de Compostela, following a pilgrimage walked for over a thousand years: the Pyrenees, Rioja, the high Meseta and green Galicia. Usually five weeks on foot, two by bike.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: French Way","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Way"}],"approximate":"Main stages; the walking path is drawn on nearby roads.","km":846,"bbox":[-8.5187,42.2676,-1.238,43.1629],"stopCount":12,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port.jpg/500px-Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port.jpg","page":"Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port.jpg","credit":"Hayden Soloviev","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"overview":[[43.1629,-1.238],[42.4588,-2.3821],[42.2676,-4.4052],[42.906,-8.5187]]},{"id":"pamir-highway","title":"Pamir Highway (M41)","who":"Classic overland route","when":"Best from June to September","vehicle":"Adventure motorcycles, bicycles and 4x4s","kind":"moto","color":"#7c2d12","summary":"About 1,200 km across the \"Roof of the World\" from Osh in Kyrgyzstan to Dushanbe in Tajikistan, over passes above 4,600 m, past high lakes and along the Afghan border on the Panj river. One of the great overland roads.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Pamir Highway","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pamir_Highway"}],"approximate":"Main places on the road; the line between them is approximate. Permits (GBAO) are needed.","km":1269,"bbox":[68.7865,37.4856,74.0479,40.5464],"stopCount":8,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Osh_03-2016_img27_view_from_Sulayman_Mountain.jpg/500px-Osh_03-2016_img27_view_from_Sulayman_Mountain.jpg","page":"Osh","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osh_03-2016_img27_view_from_Sulayman_Mountain.jpg","credit":"A.Savin","license":"FAL"},"overview":[[40.5174,72.8053],[40.2577,73.49],[39.7501,73.1507],[38.5753,73.546],[38.3841,74.0299],[37.8836,73.8508],[37.491,71.5492],[38.2561,71.3745],[38.747,70.6237],[38.5767,68.7865]]},{"id":"estrada-nacional-2","title":"Estrada Nacional 2 (Portugal)","who":"Classic road trip","when":"Best in spring and autumn","vehicle":"Motorcycle, car or bicycle","kind":"moto","color":"#166534","summary":"Portugal's longest road, 739 km from Chaves near Spain to Faro on the Algarve, through vineyards of the Douro, the forests of the centre and the open plains of the Alentejo. Known as Portugal's Route 66.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Estrada Nacional 2","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Estrada_Nacional_2"}],"approximate":"Main towns on the road; the line follows today's roads.","km":729,"bbox":[-8.2849,37.0163,-7.4554,41.7398],"stopCount":15,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Monumento_a_Carvalho_Ara%C3%BAjo_-_Vila_Real_-_Portugal_%28117679264%29.jpg/500px-Monumento_a_Carvalho_Ara%C3%BAjo_-_Vila_Real_-_Portugal_%28117679264%29.jpg","page":"Vila Real","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monumento_a_Carvalho_Ara%C3%BAjo_-_Vila_Real_-_Portugal_%28117679264%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"},"overview":[[41.7398,-7.4712],[40.2366,-8.2849],[37.0163,-7.9353]]},{"id":"camino-portugues-coastal","title":"Camino Portugués, coastal way","who":"Classic route · about half of all Portuguese Camino pilgrims in 2025","when":"Best April–June and September–October","vehicle":"On foot, 12–15 days","kind":"walk","color":"#1d4ed8","summary":"Porto to Santiago de Compostela along the Atlantic: boardwalks, beaches and fishing towns through northern Portugal, a ferry over the Minho into Galicia, then the bays of Vigo and Pontevedra before joining the central route to the cathedral. Flat, social and easy to plan, with albergues every few kilometres.","sources":[{"label":"Julie Dawn Fox: the Litoral Way (2025 walk)","url":"https://juliedawnfox.com/litoral-way-coastal-camino-portugal/"},{"label":"Stingy Nomads: Coastal Route stages (2026 guide)","url":"https://stingynomads.com/portuguese-coastal-camino-stages/"}],"approximate":"Usual stages from recent guides and reports; the path follows the marked way only approximately.","km":271,"bbox":[-8.8865,41.1429,-8.5458,42.8805],"stopCount":13,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Porto%2C_S%C3%A9_do_Porto_%289%29.jpg/500px-Porto%2C_S%C3%A9_do_Porto_%289%29.jpg","page":"Porto Cathedral","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Porto%2C_S%C3%A9_do_Porto_%289%29.jpg","credit":"Laszlo Daroczy from Miskolc, Hungary","license":"CC BY 2.0"},"overview":[[41.1429,-8.6112],[42.0266,-8.8849],[42.8805,-8.5458]]},{"id":"west-highland-way","title":"West Highland Way","who":"Classic route · Scotland's best-known long walk","when":"Best May–September (midges from June)","vehicle":"On foot, 5–8 days","kind":"walk","color":"#4338ca","summary":"About 154 km from the edge of Glasgow to Fort William at the foot of Ben Nevis: the bonnie banks of Loch Lomond, old drove and military roads, the empty moor of Rannoch and the Devil's Staircase into Glen Coe country. Inns, bunkhouses and wild camping all the way.","sources":[{"label":"Jodi Bez: West Highland Way, July 2025 (Substack)","url":"https://jodibez.substack.com/p/day-5-i-did-it-my-way"},{"label":"Grant's Tracks: day by day","url":"https://grantstracks.com/posts/whw-day1/"}],"approximate":"The usual overnight stops; the line follows paths near the waymarked route.","km":159,"bbox":[-5.1139,55.9412,-4.3176,56.8218],"stopCount":9,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/The_Square%2C_Drymen.jpg/500px-The_Square%2C_Drymen.jpg","page":"Drymen","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Square%2C_Drymen.jpg","credit":"Kenneth Allen","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"},"overview":[[55.9412,-4.3176],[56.8164,-5.1139]]},{"id":"tour-du-mont-blanc","title":"Tour du Mont Blanc","who":"Classic route · France, Italy and Switzerland on foot","when":"Late June to early September, when the huts are open","vehicle":"On foot, 7–11 days, refuges","kind":"walk","color":"#0f766e","summary":"A loop of about 170 km and 10,000 m of climbing round the Mont Blanc massif, through three countries: high cols, glaciers in view almost every day, and nights in mountain refuges where dinner is shared. Book the huts months ahead.","sources":[{"label":"Patrick Lam: TMB trip report, July–August 2025","url":"https://patricklam.ca/post/20250824-tmb"},{"label":"Kenji Saito: TMB day by day (September 2025)","url":"https://kenjisaito.com/tour-du-mont-blanc-tmb-day-2"}],"approximate":"The classic anticlockwise stages; the line follows mountain paths near the official route.","km":151,"bbox":[6.7066,45.7224,7.1281,46.0577],"stopCount":12,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Les_Houches.jpg/500px-Les_Houches.jpg","page":"Les Houches","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Les_Houches.jpg","credit":"Florival fr","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"overview":[[45.8915,6.799],[45.8915,6.799]]},{"id":"pacific-crest-trail","title":"Pacific Crest Trail","who":"Classic route · Mexico to Canada on foot","when":"Northbound, late April to September","vehicle":"On foot, 4–6 months","kind":"walk","color":"#a16207","summary":"About 4,265 km from the Mexican border to Canada through California, Oregon and Washington: desert, the High Sierra, volcanoes and old forest. A few thousand people start each year; most hike northbound, timing the desert before summer and the Sierra after the snow.","sources":[{"label":"Halfway Anywhere: PCT best moments, class of 2025","url":"https://www.halfwayanywhere.com/trails/pacific-crest-trail/pct-best-moments-2025/"},{"label":"Halfway Anywhere: PCT tips from the class of 2025","url":"https://www.halfwayanywhere.com/trails/pacific-crest-trail/pacific-crest-trail-tips-2025-2026/"}],"approximate":"The usual resupply towns and landmarks; the line follows trails near the PCT where they were found.","km":3852,"bbox":[-122.7154,32.5897,-116.4125,49.1566],"stopCount":24,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Julian_Californien.JPG/500px-Julian_Californien.JPG","page":"Julian, California","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Julian_Californien.JPG","credit":"--Microsomen 17:11, 31 May 2005 (UTC)","license":"CC BY 2.0"},"overview":[[32.5897,-116.4669],[34.1035,-116.6796],[35.1322,-118.4491],[35.6728,-117.8746],[36.9201,-118.2363],[40.0384,-121.401],[40.9905,-121.5932],[42.0734,-122.6947],[43.7104,-121.4403],[45.7955,-121.9906],[48.4749,-120.71],[49.1566,-120.8553]]},{"id":"north-coast-500","title":"North Coast 500","who":"Classic route · Scotland's Highland loop by motorcycle","when":"Best May or September–October","vehicle":"Motorcycle (or car, camper, bike), 5–7 days","kind":"moto","color":"#be185d","summary":"A loop of about 830 km from Inverness round the far north of Scotland: the Bealach na Bà pass, empty single-track roads along sea lochs, white beaches, mountains like Suilven and Stac Pollaidh, and the cliffs of the north coast. Use the passing places and expect four seasons a day.","sources":[{"label":"Horizons Unlimited: a beginner's take on the NC500","url":"https://www.horizonsunlimited.com/hubb/ride-tales/beginners-take-on-the-nc500-93251"},{"label":"Wheelworld: five on tour, mostly on two wheels","url":"https://www.wheelworldreviews.co.uk/?p=18615"}],"approximate":"The usual anticlockwise loop and overnight towns.","km":811,"bbox":[-5.813,57.3969,-3.069,58.6483],"stopCount":12,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg/500px-Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","page":"Inverness","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","credit":"Diliff","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"overview":[[57.4793,-4.2261],[57.4793,-4.2261]]},{"id":"ha-giang-loop","title":"Ha Giang Loop","who":"Classic route · northern Vietnam by motorbike","when":"Best October–November (buckwheat flowers) and March–May","vehicle":"Motorbike or with an easy rider, 3–4 days","kind":"moto","color":"#c2410c","summary":"A loop of 350–450 km through the karst mountains on the Chinese border: the Ma Pi Leng pass above the Nho Que river, Hmong villages and markets, terraced valleys and homestays. Most go anticlockwise from Ha Giang; many ride pillion with a local driver.","sources":[{"label":"Kreier: the Ha Giang Loop a second time (2025)","url":"https://kreier.github.io/quartz/Travel/2025/Ha-Giang-loop-a-second-time-in-2025"},{"label":"Team-BHP travelogue: Ha Giang Loop (May 2025)","url":"https://www.team-bhp.com/forum/travelogues/294466-ha-giang-loop-vietnam.html"}],"approximate":"The usual anticlockwise loop and overnight villages.","km":448,"bbox":[104.929,22.7315,105.5482,23.3625],"stopCount":10,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Thitrantamson.jpg/500px-Thitrantamson.jpg","page":"Quản Bạ district","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thitrantamson.jpg","credit":"Thái Nhi at vi.wikipedia","license":"Public domain"},"overview":[[22.8175,104.9506],[22.8175,104.9506]]},{"id":"annapurna-circuit","title":"Annapurna Circuit","who":"Classic route · round the Annapurna massif","when":"Best October–November and March–May","vehicle":"On foot, 10–16 days, teahouses","kind":"walk","color":"#9333ea","summary":"From the green Marsyangdi valley up through Buddhist villages to Manang, over the Thorong La pass at 5,416 m and down to the pilgrimage temples of Muktinath and the deep Kali Gandaki gorge. Teahouses all the way; the acclimatisation days in Manang matter.","sources":[{"label":"Dave's Travel Corner: Annapurna Circuit journal (July 2025)","url":"https://www.davestravelcorner.com/?p=139934"},{"label":"Explore-Share: 11-day itinerary, lodges and food","url":"https://www.explore-share.com/blog/annapurna-circuit-eleven-day-itinerary-route-lodges-food/"}],"approximate":"The usual stages anticlockwise; the line follows trails and jeep tracks near the route.","km":242,"bbox":[83.5948,28.231,84.4144,28.8412],"stopCount":12,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Besi_Sahar.JPG/500px-Besi_Sahar.JPG","page":"Besishahar","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Besi_Sahar.JPG","credit":"Dmitry A. Mottl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"overview":[[28.231,84.3762],[28.84,83.819],[28.2981,83.7678]]},{"id":"gibb-river-road","title":"Gibb River Road","who":"Classic route · the Kimberley by 4x4","when":"Dry season only, about May–October","vehicle":"4x4, 7–14 days, bush camping","kind":"4x4","color":"#b45309","summary":"About 660 km of mostly dirt road across the Kimberley in Western Australia, an old cattle route between Derby and Kununurra: red gorges with swimming holes, river crossings like the Pentecost, cattle stations with campgrounds, and very few people. Carry fuel, water and two spare tyres.","sources":[{"label":"Andy & Ness: the Gibb River Road, part III (September 2025)","url":"https://andyandnessas-allaussieadventures.blogspot.com/2025/09/the-gibb-river-road-part-iii.html"},{"label":"Australia.com: Gibb River Road itinerary","url":"https://australia.com/en/trips-and-itineraries/broome-and-surrounds/the-gibb-river-road-itinerary.html"}],"approximate":"The usual west-to-east stops; the line follows the road where the router found it.","km":1079,"bbox":[122.2237,-17.9562,128.7391,-15.7235],"stopCount":9,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Broome%2C_Western_Australia_11.jpg/500px-Broome%2C_Western_Australia_11.jpg","page":"Broome, Western Australia","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broome%2C_Western_Australia_11.jpg","credit":"Kat Clay from Sydney, Australia","license":"CC BY 2.0"},"overview":[[-17.956,122.2237],[-17.7381,123.6429],[-17.3028,123.629],[-17.412,124.9432],[-15.9472,126.8279],[-15.7732,128.7391]]},{"id":"lagunas-route","title":"Lagunas Route: Uyuni to San Pedro de Atacama","who":"Classic route · the Bolivian Altiplano by bike","when":"Best April–November (dry, very cold nights)","vehicle":"Bikepacking (also motorcycle or 4x4), 7–12 days","kind":"bike","color":"#0891b2","summary":"Sandy, corrugated tracks over 4,000–5,000 m through south-west Bolivia: coloured lagoons full of flamingos, geysers, hot springs and volcanoes, then a fast drop of 2,000 m into Chile's Atacama desert. Remote and hard: carry food, water and warm clothes.","sources":[{"label":"Bikepacking.com: Lagunas y Salares route","url":"https://bikepacking.com/routes/lagunas-y-salares/"},{"label":"Itchy Boots: 10 tips for the Ruta de las Lagunas","url":"https://www.itchyboots.com/bikers-guide/10-tips-for-riding-the-ruta-de-las-lagunas-in-bolivia"}],"approximate":"The usual villages, lagoons and refuges; the tracks shift every season, so the line is a guide only.","km":562,"bbox":[-68.1922,-23.3282,-66.7182,-20.4629],"stopCount":10,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Uyuni_Potosi_Ave_Aerial.jpg/500px-Uyuni_Potosi_Ave_Aerial.jpg","page":"Uyuni","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uyuni_Potosi_Ave_Aerial.jpg","credit":"Jaimalalatete","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},"overview":[[-20.4629,-66.8239],[-21.1437,-66.7448],[-21.4091,-67.6139],[-22.5785,-67.657],[-22.914,-68.1922],[-23.3282,-67.9052]]},{"id":"morocco-atlas-sahara","title":"Morocco: Atlas to Sahara","who":"Classic route · southern Morocco by motorcycle","when":"Best March–May and October–November","vehicle":"Adventure motorcycle, 7–10 days","kind":"moto","color":"#dc2626","summary":"From Marrakech over the High Atlas by the Tizi n'Tichka, past kasbahs and film-set Ouarzazate, through the Dades and Todra gorges to the dunes of Merzouga, and back by the Draa valley palm groves. Tarmac for most, with endless dirt tracks for those who want them.","sources":[{"label":"Mosko Moto: lightweight dual-sport route across Morocco (November 2025)","url":"https://moskomoto.com/blogs/mosko-moto-blog/trip-report-lightweight-dual-sport-route-across-morocco"},{"label":"Rider Magazine: Morocco adventure tour review (March 2025)","url":"https://ridermagazine.com/2025/03/07/imtbike-morocco-adventure-motorcycle-tour-review/"}],"approximate":"The usual loop and overnight towns.","km":1602,"bbox":[-7.9895,30.0298,-4.0143,31.6259],"stopCount":10,"cover":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Djemaa_el_Fna.jpg/500px-Djemaa_el_Fna.jpg","page":"Jemaa el-Fnaa","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Djemaa_el_Fna.jpg","credit":"Boris Macek","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"overview":[[31.6259,-7.9895],[31.6259,-7.9895]]}]